    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/239793": {
      "title": "Painter (53026)",
      "description": "Painter (53026) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Painter (53026) Las Vegas , NM 87701 Apply Overview Salary Range $16.54 Position Type Full Time -Reg Education Level High School or GED Category Staff Apply Description SUMMARY: Under general supervision from the General Maintenance Manager, leads planning efforts for waterproofing and painting projects. Inspects buildings and documents interior and exterior finish coating repair requirements. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Plans work; estimates job costs, and selects materials. Surveys buildings to determine repairs needed and develops schedules for completion. Applies paints, sealers, solvents, varnishes and stains to exterior and interior building surfaces such as plaster, sheetrock, concrete, furniture, and wood. Operates equipment such as airless spray equipment, scaffolding, and motorized lifts. Cleans and maintains brushes, rollers, spray units, and hand tools. Performs building exterior and interior caulking, finish repair, mud and tape, and texturing tasks. Follows all applicable local, state and federal codes and statutes in the field. Ability to understand and carry out verbal and written instructions, and performs a variety of manual tasks, as required. Uses mechanized high-reach equipment to renew caulking on exterior building panel seams, windows, and doors. Performs special refinishing tasks including wood surface preparation, staining, and sealing. Ensures proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: EDUCATION : High School Diploma or GED. EXPERIENCE: Three (3) years of experience that is directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified. EMPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS: Must possess and maintain a valid New Mexico Driver’s license. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Ability to understand and follow specific verbal and written instructions and procedures. Ability to use hand and power tools applicable to trade. Knowledge of light equipment operation and/or maintenance. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Ability to read, understand, follow, and enforce safety procedures. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Lifting 0 to 50 pounds – Frequently Standing – Frequently Walking – Frequently Bending – Frequently Squatting – Frequently Climbing – Frequently Kneeling – Frequently WORK ENVIRONMENT: May be exposed to hazardous chemicals and materials. Work in dirty/dusty conditions – Frequently Work in loud conditions – Frequently Work around fumes and odors – Frequently Work in wet and humid environment – Occasionally Work in poorly lit areas – Occasionally Work on elevated heights – Frequently Lifting greater than fifty (50) pounds with assistance – Occasionally Work in noisy conditions – Occasionally Pushing greater than fifty (50) pounds with assistance – Occasionally Pulling greater than fifty (50) pounds with assistance – Occasionally Work in extreme temperatures – Frequently Work in smoky conditions – Occasionally Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
