      "description": "Laboratory Aide (52953) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Laboratory Aide (52953) Apply Overview Salary Range $13.50 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Category Student Apply Description Primary Contact: Michael Petronis, Ph.D. Laboratory Aide III position entails assisting with the sample through-flow in the rock magnetic-paleomagnetic laboratories by 1) Conducting rock magnetic-paleomagnetic rock analyses after training by your direct supervisor in sample preparation and instrument operation. 2) Maintaining a log of research activities. 3) Updating the on-line literature database on specific projects as needed. 4) Establishing and maintaining a GIS database of studies conducted in the laboratory. 5) Performing other tasks as assigned. Qualifications Education Requirements: High School diploma; completion of GEOL 1110 or equivalant . Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
