      "description": "Warehouse Aide (52938) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Warehouse Aide (52938) Apply Overview Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Category Student Apply Description Position Summary: The Work-Study Warehouse Aide assists with accepting, receiving, coordinating and distributing packages, letters and materials through the New Mexico Highlands University campus. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: - Receiving of incoming packages from USPS, UPS and FedEx. - Operate all Central Receiving and Post-Office automated systems. - Delivery of packages to designated departments. - Assist with moving furniture, equipment, and boxes as needed. - Maintains regular attendance. - Follow university policies and workplace safety guidelines. -Perform other related duties and assigned. Qualifications Qualifications: - Must be eligible for Federal Work Study through the university's Financial Aide Office. -Current enrollment as a student at the university. - Ability to provide quality customer service. - Ability to follow verbal and written instructions. - Dependable, punctual, and able to work independently and as part of a team. - Basic computer skills preferred. Physical Requirements: - Sitting.........-Occasionally - Bending------Frequently - Standing-----Frequently - Walking------Frequently - Squatting----Frequently - Kneeling-----Frequently - Climbing-----Frequently - Lifting/carrying up to (fifty) 50 pounds------Frequently - Lifting/carrying over (fifty) 50 pounds-------Frequently Pay Rate: According to university work-study guidelines. Work Schedule: Flexible around class schedules. up tp the maximum hours permitted by the Work-Study Program Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be en