    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/235309": {
      "title": "Supplemental Instruction Leader (SIL)(Student) (52731)",
      "description": "Supplemental Instruction Leader (SIL)(Student) (52731) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Supplemental Instruction Leader (SIL)(Student) (52731) Apply Overview Salary Range $13.50 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description Primary contact: Jonathan Lujan, SIL Coordinator jonathanlujan@nmhu.edu The SI Leader is a peer academic support role that provides regularly scheduled, out-of-class study sessions for students enrolled in historically challenging STEM courses. SI Leaders attend the target course alongside enrolled students, model effective study strategies, and facilitate collaborative session s that reinforce course content ans build students; independent learning skills. Qualifications Currently enrolled NMHU Student in good academic standing Earned an A or B in the target course (or equivalent, as approved by the SI Coordinator) Strong communication, organization, and interpersonal skills Reliable, responsible, and able to commit to a consistent weekly schedule Prior tutoring or leadership helpful but not required Preferred Qualifications: Currently enrolled NMHU Student in good academic standing Earned an A or B in the target course (or equivalent, as approved by the SI Coordinator) Strong communication, organization, and interpersonal skills Reliable, responsible, and able to commit to a consistent weekly schedule Prior tutoring or leadership helpful but not required Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
