    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/235081": {
      "title": "Chief of Police (52726)",
      "description": "Chief of Police (52726) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Chief of Police (52726) Las Vegas , NM 87701 Apply Overview Salary Range $78,790.40 - $96,793.00 Salary Position Type Full Time -Reg Education Level High School or GED Category Staff Apply Description SUMMARY: This position is the Chief Administrative Officer of the Department and has authority in all matters of Police and Fire Safety Operations including discipline as per authorization and jurisdiction set forth by state statute and designated by the Board of Regents, see Administrative Policy 100. He/she exercises all lawful powers of his/her office and issues such lawful orders as are necessary to assure the effective performance of the department. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: • Ensures preparation of periodic and special reports, and assures that adequate records are maintained of all department activities. • Responsible for the department’s continued and efficient operation, for the enforcement of rules and regulations within the department, for the completion and forwarding of such reports as may be required by proper authority and for the department’s relations with local citizens, the local government, and other related agencies. • Plans, directs, coordinates, controls and staffing all activities of the department. • Enforces all laws coming within the department’s legal jurisdiction. • Controls the expenditures of department appropriations and prepares annual budget estimates of needs. • Ensure cooperation with other law enforcement agencies in the apprehension and detention of wanted persons and with other agencies as appropriate. • Receives, evaluates and resolves complaints; attends civic club and school meetings to explain the activities and functions of the police department, and to establish favorable public relations. • Formulates written administrative guidance in the form of policies, regulations and other orders governing activities of the Police Department. • Ensures compliance with all laws, which the department or its officers have the authority to enforce. • Organizes, directs, and controls all resources of the department to preserve the peace, protect persons and property and enforce the law. • Designates a Commander to serve as Commanding Officer in his absence. • Assigns or transfers any member or employee of the department to or from any assignment whenever he/she shall deem such action necessary for the efficiency, discipline or morale of the department. • Investigates all cases of alleged or apparent misconduct by department personnel. • Keeps himself/herself informed of departmental affairs, ensuring that the duties and responsibilities of members and employees are properly discharged. • Promulgates all General and Special orders of the department and issued on this own authority orders, written and oral, consistent with his/her powers, duties and responsibilities. • Maintains a personnel record system in which shall be kept all pertinent information on all departmental members and employees. • Works with Facilities Services to schedule required annual fire system and equipment maintenance/inspections. • Maintains a record system in which shall be kept all pertinent information on all required fire inspections and maintenance. • Maintains regular attendance. • Performs other job-related duties as assigned. WORK ENVIRONMENT: • May be exposed to hazardous chemicals and materials – Occasionally • Work in dirty/dusty conditions – Occasionally • Work in noisy conditions – Occasionally • Work around fumes and odors – Occasionally • Work in wet and humid environments – Occasionally • Work in poorly lit areas – Occasionally • Work on elevated heights – Seldom • Work out of a vehicle – Frequently Qualifications MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: • EDUCATION: High School Diploma or GED. • EXPERIENCE: Five (5) years of certified law enforcement experience, two (2) of which must include supervisory experience. o PREFERENCE: • • EMPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS: • Must possess and maintain a valid NM Drivers License. • Possess New Mexico Police Certification, or obtain recertification within 1 year. • Must be at least 18 years of age. • Be free of any felony or domestic violence conviction. • Must be willing to work evenings, weekends, holidays, odd hours, and emergency calls. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: • Comprehensive knowledge of laws, rules, and court decisions relating to the administration of criminal justice and law enforcement. • Knowledge of scientific methods of crime detection, criminal identification and radio communication. • Comprehensive knowledge of controlling laws and ordinances. • Demonstrated ability to lead and direct the activities of police officers. • Ability to maintain cooperative relationships with others and with the general public. • Ability to evaluate the effectiveness of the police operation and to institute improvements. • Ability to prepare and review reports; resourcefulness and sound judgment and emergencies. • Ability to demonstrate integrity and tact. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: • Lifting 0 to 50 pounds – Frequently • Lifting greater than fifty (50) pounds – Seldom • Standing –Frequently • Walking – Frequently • Bending – Frequently • Squatting – Frequently • Climbing – Frequently • Kneeling – Occasionally • Running – Occasionally • Sitting – Frequently Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/234771": {
      "title": "Contingent Faculty - Art (52680)",
      "description": "Contingent Faculty - Art (52680) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Contingent Faculty - Art (52680) Apply Overview Salary Range $1,050.00 Commission Position Type Faculty - Per Course Education Level Masters Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Job Summary New Mexico Highlands University seeks a Contingent Faculty member in Art to teach ART 1120: Introduction to Art as a Dual Credit course at Robertson High School in Las Vegas, New Mexico. The successful candidate will provide quality instruction, maintain appropriate academic standards, evaluate student performance, and support student success in accordance with NMHU policies and curriculum requirements. This is a per-course, temporary faculty appointment for the Fall 2026 semester. Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Art, Art History, Studio Art, Fine Arts, or a closely related field. Prior college-level or dual credit teaching experience. Experience teaching introductory art courses. Experience working with diverse student populations, including high school students. Demonstrated commitment to student engagement and academic success. Preferred Skills Preferred Skills Strong verbal and written communication skills. Effective classroom management and organizational skills. Ability to incorporate contemporary and interdisciplinary approaches to art education. Proficiency with instructional technologies and online learning platforms. Ability to work collaboratively with university faculty, administrators, and secondary education partners. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Essential Duties Teach ART 1120: Introduction to Art in accordance with approved course outcomes. Prepare and deliver engaging lectures, discussions, and course activities. Assess student learning and maintain accurate academic records. Submit grades and required reports in a timely manner. Maintain regular communication with students, high school personnel, and the NMHU Art and Music Department. Comply with university policies, procedures, and accreditation standards. [Paycom Job...school Art | Word] Physical Demands Ability to stand, walk, and instruct for extended periods. Ability to communicate effectively in classroom settings. Ability to use computers, instructional technology, and standard office equipment. May require occasional lifting or moving of classroom art materials and supplies up to 25 pounds. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
