    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/213000": {
      "title": "Contingent Faculty - Counseling (51716)",
      "description": "Contingent Faculty - Counseling (51716) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Contingent Faculty - Counseling (51716) Las Vegas, NM 87701 Apply Overview Salary Range $1,050.00 Commission Position Type Faculty - Per Course Education Level Masters Degree Travel Percentage None Category Faculty Apply Description The NMHU Counseling Department is seeking applicants for per course faculty. Per course faculty typically teach 3-6 credits per semester, with class schedules determined based on departmental needs and candidate availability. Courses are taught online either asynchronous, ZOOM, or asynchronous and ZOOM. Per course positions remain posted continuously to expand the Counseling program's pool of qualified per course faculty. Screening of applications will commence when an open position becomes available within the program. Should a position become available, you will receive an email advising you of the next steps. This is a REMOTE Position. For additional information about the department, please visit the NMHU Counseling Department web page at: https://www.nmhu.edu/landing-counseling/ New Mexico Highlands University requires all applications and supporting documents to be submitted via the university's Paycom portal. The following documents are required: --Resume or Curriculum Vitae --Cover Letter --Contact Information and Three Professional References --Two Letters of Recommendation Optional documents: NONE Special Instructions for Applicants: We encourage applicants to include information in the cover letter that addresses their approach to teaching and their plans to advance diversity, equity, and inclusion in their position at NMHU. Term Faculty Responsibilities: Teach 3 (1 course) - 6 (2 courses) credits during a semester. Teaches assigned course(s) online, delivering appropriate course content to students, preparing course materials, lesson plans and setting up the gradebook in Brightspace that correspond to assignments. Teaches assigned course(s) online by delivering course content, learning activities and assessment using the university's learning management system. Grade student work and provide students with robust feedback in a timely manner. Develop and deliver course lectures and/or materials by ZOOM and Brightspace. Discussions and assignments are outlined in the course syllabus and are in accordance with the curriculum and learning objectives. Maintain accurate records of student attendance, academic achievement, and performance in accordance with university policies and procedures. Distribute to each student, in each course, via the learning management system, a department approved syllabus that includes course objectives, required course materials, attendance policy, evaluation criteria, accessibility services, and other required information. Communicate early with the student, department chair, and academic advisor for any student at risk of failure or in need of individual counseling using appropriate university services. Respond to students by email/phone within 24 hours during weekdays. Provide time as needed to meet with students outside of class, including virtual office hours. Foster a positive and inclusive learning environment conducive to student engagement and academic success. Develop and administer projects and exams to evaluate student learning outcomes and provide grades in a timely manner. Some courses have a \"Key Performance Measures\" assignment that needs to be graded on the Experiential Learning Cloud (ELC). Provide timely feedback and guidance to students to support their learning and development. Share any questions or concerns in a timely manner with the Counseling Department Chair. Performs other duties as assigned. Term Faculty Requirements: Master's degree in counseling from a CACREP Accredited Program. Prior teaching experience with master's level counseling students on an online learning platform. Professional experiences as a counselor. Current counselor licensure. Innovative thinker with strong conceptual and problem-solving skills. Strong organizational and planning skills. Ability to work under pressure and react effectively. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in counseling, from a CACREP Accredited Program and 2 years of professional experience in the counseling field practicing as a counselor. Current counselor licensure. Professional, self-starter, and strong work ethic. Experience with online learning platforms, including experience teaching on online learning platforms. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Counselor Education from a CACREP accredited institution. Experience working with mental health professionals, clients, and master's level students in counseling. Preferred Skills Ability to work independently and make sound informed decisions. Excellent communication and problem-solving skills. Doesn't hesitate to reach out for assistance when needed. Knowledge of CACREP accreditation standards and online learning best practices. Experience using online learning platforms and setting up classes on Brightspace. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/229461": {
      "title": "Recreation Aide (52389)",
      "description": "Recreation Aide (52389) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Recreation Aide (52389) Apply Overview Salary Range $12.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description Under the direct supervision of the Assistant Director of Student Life, the Recreation Aide serves as a leader within the Campus Recreation program. This position responsible for overseeing Game Room operations, supervising Game room Attendants, assisting with recreational programming, officiating intramural sports, and supporting student events. Recreation Aides help create a fun, inclusive, and safe environment while providing excellent customer service to students. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Arrive on time and prepare for all scheduled shifts. Assist with recruiting, hiring, training, scheduling, supervising, and evaluating Game Room Attendants. Maintain inventory of video games,  gaming systems, equipment, and supplies. Monitor Game Room operations during assigned shifts. Check out games, controllers, and equipment to participants. Keep the Game Room clean, organized, and welcoming. Report equipment damage and maintenance needs to the supervisor. Submit marketing requests for upcoming programs and events. Respond to emergencies according to First Aid/CPR training and university procedures. Attend Campus Recreation Leadership meeting and conduct Game Room staff meetings. Maintain accurate records of hours worked and submit times sheets by required deadlines. Officiate intramural sports contests. Assist with pre-game and post-game logistics and administrative duties. Prepare and inspect game sites before activities begin. Understand and follow emergency and evacuation procedures. Promote Campus Recreation programs and educate participants on policies. Verify participants eligibility for intramural competitions. Attend all requires official  training clinics. Provide exceptional customer service in a friendly and professional manner. Assist with Arts@HU events and other campus programs. Advertise and promote student events. Perform other duties as assigned. Physical Demands: Ability to stand and walk for extended periods. Ability to lift and move recreational equipment (up to approximately 25-50 pounds as needed). Ability to demonstrate and officiate recreational sports activities. Ability to work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and daytime shifts. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Current enrolled student in good academic standings. Current First Aid and CPR/AED certifications or willingness to obtain certifications. Knowledge of video gaming systems, equipment, and connectivity. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to maintain a professional and positive attitude. Willingness to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience as a Game Room Attendant. Previous intramural sports officiating experience. Previous customer service experience. Experience supervising or leading peers. Knowledge of intramural sports rules and Campus Recreation policies. Preferred Skills: Strong leadership and supervisory abilities. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple responsibilities simultaneously. Strong organizational and time management skills. Experience promoting programs and events through marketing and outreach. Demonstrated knowledge of recreational programming and student engagement. Exemplary officiating experience in tow or more intramural sports seasons. Ability to create a welcoming, inclusive, and engaging environment for participants. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
