    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/228401": {
      "title": "Research Aide V (52404)",
      "description": "Research Aide V (52404) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Research Aide V (52404) Apply Overview Salary Range $14.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description Primary Contact: Dylin Montoya Email: dylinmontoya@nmhu.edu Job Summary/Description/Physical Demands: Students hired through this posting will support NMHU's Department of Forestry, as well as the related efforts of the New Mexico Reforestation Center. Duties assigned to this position may include both on campus and field assignments that support the Department of Forestry and/or New Mexico Reforestation Center objectives and deliverables. Individuals hired under this posting will also have the potential to serve as Reforestation Technicians and Nursery Trainees for the New Mexico Reforestation Center. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Education: College Student at NMHU, enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours High School Diploma or GED Experience: No experience to some clerical/office experience Preferred Qualifications: Students currently enrolled in the B.S. in Forestry or B.A. on Conservative Management programs will be preferred. Individuals with prior experience in field research, technical tree climbing, seed collection, seed processing, nursery production environments, and/pr tree planting will be preferred. Current NMHU defensive driver training is preferred, but training will be provided if needed. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
