    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/228332": {
      "title": "Peer Advisor / Tutor (52399)",
      "description": "Peer Advisor / Tutor (52399) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Peer Advisor / Tutor (52399) Apply Overview Salary Range $13.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description Position may include varied and moderately complex duties involving a moderate degree of responsibility and judgement. Usually requires previous training or equivalent experience. May direct or coordinate activities of other student employees. A Peer Mentor is a leader who helps ease the transitions to college for new students by creating a community in which new students feel a sense of belonging and support. Peer Mentors are embedded into First Year Experience FYEX 1110, Learning Community classes, and courses they have previously taken. They provide mentoring, tutoring, and study sessions services, connect students to campus resources, conduct students surveys, and manage student information. Outside of scheduled classes, Peer Mentors organize and lead social academic events. Physical Description: Help first-year students and peers' transition and succeed at college. Help students connect to campus resources. Serve as a positive mentor and role model, academically and behaviorally. Develop, proved, and maintain effective working relationships, assistance, and support. Establish regular communication with students through email, text, social media, etc. Regularly attend assigned weekly classes, participate in and lead class activities, and take notes. Meet and collaborate with faculty. Attend department staff meetings and trainings. Hold office hours for tutoring and mentoring services. Organize and facilitate study groups. Plan and facilitate events and activities with students outside of class. Create and distribute marketing media. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Is classified as a college sophomore, junior or senior Is in good academic and disciplinary standing. Has a 3.0 GPA or higher. Enrolled in a minimum of six (6) credit hours. Preferred Qualifications: Has a genuine willingness or desire to help their peers succeed. Exhibits a high level of motivation, initiative, and personal responsibility. Exhibits interpersonal skills. communication skills. Can maintain effective working relationships. Effective in time management , and organization. Able to keep regular attendance. Able to relate to people from diverse backgrounds and willingness to learn about different cultures. Demonstrates leadership potential. Preferred Skills: A background in mentoring and tutoring, or a willingness to learn. Able to design graphics for physical and digital media, or a willingness to learn. Navigate and post on social media platforms, or a willingness to learn. Ability  to write professional emails. or willingness to learn. Can use a campus Microsoft 360 suite, campus portal, and campus apps. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
