    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/213703": {
      "title": "Student Services Aide (51736)",
      "description": "Student Services Aide (51736) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student Services Aide (51736) Apply Overview Salary Range $12.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description The Student Services Aide provides front‑line administrative and customer service support for the Student Services office. This role assists students, faculty, staff, and visitors while contributing to efficient office operations. The position also plays an active role in supporting new student orientation and other student‑focused programs. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Serve as a first point of contact by greeting and assisting students, visitors, faculty, and staff in person, by phone, and via email Answer inquiries, provide general information, and refer individuals to appropriate offices or personnel Perform clerical and administrative tasks, including filing, data entry, copying, scanning, and document preparation Assist with scheduling appointments, meetings, and events Assist with new student orientation , including check‑in, event setup, information distribution, and providing general support to new students and families Maintain student records and handle information in compliance with FERPA and university confidentiality policies Support daily office operations, special projects, and university events as assigned Use standard office equipment and software, including computers, printers, and Microsoft Office applications Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Must be currently enrolled as a student in good academic standing High school diploma or GED Strong customer service and communication skills Basic computer proficiency Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a professional office environment Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow university policies and procedures Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
