    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/178726": {
      "title": "Contingent Faculty - Computer Science (50322)",
      "description": "Contingent Faculty - Computer Science (50322) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Contingent Faculty - Computer Science (50322) Las Vegas , NM 87701 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level Masters Degree Category Faculty Apply Description Position Summary The incumbent in this position will have responsibilities in the areas of teaching, scholarship and service. Courses to be taught will be primarily in the areas of network programming, cybersecurity, database theory, web programming, software engineering, data structures, algorithm development, data-science but may include classes taught outside of those topics, depending on expertise Duties and Responsibilities Faculty contractual duties include, but are not limited to: • Teach courses in graduate and undergraduate CS programs. • May be assigned to teach evening and/or Saturday classes, courses via ITV, and/or develop and teach Desire to Learn courses; • Hold office hours as required; • Maintain regular attendance; $1050 per credit hour Qualifications Education: Masters or Doctorate in Computer Science or a closely related field or equivalent credentials. Doctoral candidates that have completed all but their dissertation are also qualified. Experience: University experience in teaching computer science courses as an instructor or assistant. Preferred Qualifications In addition to the minimum qualifications, preference will be given to the following:  Expertise in several of the following areas: network programming,cybersecurity, database theory, web programming, software engineering, data structures, algorithm development and data-science.  University experience in teaching undergraduate and graduate courses  Demonstrated research activities in the broad field of computer and information science  Previous success in working with diverse student populations  Interest and/or experience implementing curricula and/or pedagogy in discipline  Experience interacting with multicultural communities Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Skill and expertise in delivering computer science content and coursework to diverse students. • Ability in the use of classroom technologies and/or strategies to enhance pedagogy. • Ability to work effectively with colleagues, administrators and a culturally diverse student body. • Ability to demonstrate excellent written and oral communication skills. • Ability to supervise undergraduate and graduate student projects. • Demonstrated skill and ability in writing software programs. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/2881FFE43C19E2921F626A9C2B366153/jobs/216323": {
      "title": "Recycling Aide (51880)",
      "description": "Recycling Aide (51880) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Recycling Aide (51880) Apply Overview Salary Range $12.00 - $14.00 Hourly Position Type Part Time - Reg Education Level High School or GED Travel Percentage None Category Student Apply Description The person in this position is responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of the Recycling Aide duties DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Under the general direction of the Set-Ups/Custodial/Recycling Manager, this position is expected to: Collect and transport recyclable materials from designated locations across campus. Sort and separate recyclable items such as cardboard, paper, plastic, aluminum, and glass according to recycling guidelines. Operate recycling equipment to create and prepare bales of recyclable materials for storage or transport. Maintain cleanliness and organization of the recycling yard and work areas to ensure a safe environment. Pick up and empty recycling bins throughout campus on a scheduled basis. Assist with loading, unloading, and storing recyclable materials. Inspect materials to remove contamination and ensure proper recycling procedures are followed. Follow all campus safety policies and proper lifting techniques while performing duties. Report equipment issues, safety hazards, or supply needs to supervisors. Support campus sustainability and environmental initiatives through responsible recycling practices. Other tasks as assigned Physical Demands: Lifting 0 to 50 pounds……………………………………………………..Frequently Lifting greater than 50 pounds……………………….…………………Frequently Standing………………………………………………………….……………Frequently Walking…………………………………….……………………….…………Frequently Bending………………………………………..………………………………Frequently Squatting………………………………………………………………………Frequently Climbng…………………………………………………………..……………Frequently Kneeling………………………………………………………………………..Frequently Working Environment: Work in dirty/dusty conditions……………………………………………Frequently Work in noisy conditions……………………………………………….…Frequently Work around fumes and odors………………………………………….…Frequently Work in wet and humid environments….…………………………….…Frequently Work in poorly lit areas…………………………………..……….……….…Frequently Work on elevated heights……………………………………..………….…Frequently Qualifications Minimum Qualifications EDUCATION: Must be registered and enrolled in a New Mexico Highlands University Program. EXPERIENCE: Previous experience in recycling matters is preferred but not required Preferred Qualifications None Preferred Skills Strong organizational and time management skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Knowledge of basic recycling procedures and material identification. Ability to safely lift, carry, and move heavy materials. Strong attention to detail when sorting recyclable items. Dependable, punctual, and responsible work habits. Good communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to operate basic recycling and cleaning equipment safely. Problem-solving skills and ability to follow instructions. Commitment to maintaining a clean and safe work environment. Share job details to About NEW MEXICO HIGHLANDS UNIVERSITY Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
